ask","kuuliza","koo-oo-LEE-zah"],["to answer","kujibu","koo-JEE-boo"],["to repeat","kurudia","koo-roo-DEE-ah"],["to understand","kuelewa","koo-eh-LEH-wah"],["to remember","kukumbuka","koo-koom-BOO-kah"],["to forget","kusahau","koo-sah-HAH-oo"],["to explain","kueleza","koo-eh-LEH-zah"],["to practise","kufanya mazoezi","koo-FAHN-yah mah-zoh-EH-zee"],["to pass an exam","kufaulu mtihani","koo-fah-OO-loo m-tee-HAH-nee"],["to fail an exam","kufeli mtihani","koo-FEH-lee m-tee-HAH-nee"],["to write down","kuandika","koo-ahn-DEE-kah"],["to listen","kusikiliza","koo-see-kee-LEE-zah"],["to read aloud","kusoma kwa sauti","koo-SOH-mah kwah sah-OO-tee"],["to think","kufikiri","koo-fee-KEE-ree"],["to count","kuhesabu","koo-heh-SAH-boo"],["to spell","kutaja herufi","koo-TAH-jah heh-ROO-fee"],["to translate","kutafsiri","koo-tahf-SEE-ree"],["to graduate","kuhitimu","koo-hee-TEE-moo"]]}],"grammar":[{"id":"pronouns","title":"Pronouns","text":["Swahili has no he / she difference: \"yeye\" means both. The pronoun is also built into the verb, so it is often left out. Learn the verb prefixes: ni- (I), u- (you), a- (he, she), tu- (we), m- (you plural), wa- (they)."],"rows":[["I","mimi","MEE-mee"],["you","wewe","WEH-weh"],["he / she","yeye","YEH-yeh"],["we","sisi","SEE-see"],["you (plural)","ninyi","NEE-nyee"],["they","wao","WAH-oh"]],"ex":[["I am a student","mimi ni mwanafunzi","MEE-mee nee mwah-nah-FOON-zee"],["you are tall","wewe ni mrefu","WEH-weh nee m-REH-foo"],["she is my older sister","yeye ni dada yangu mkubwa","YEH-yeh nee DAH-dah YAHN-goo m-KOO-bwah"],["we are friends","sisi ni marafiki","SEE-see nee mah-rah-FEE-kee"],["they are teachers","wao ni walimu","WAH-oh nee wah-LEE-moo"]]},{"id":"singular-and-plural","title":"Singular and plural","text":["The plural changes the first part of the noun, according to its class. Person: m- to wa- (mtu, watu). Thing: ki- to vi- (kitabu, vitabu). Many nouns: n- stays the same (nyumba, nyumba). Tree: m- to mi- (mti, miti)."],"rows":[["person, people","mtu, watu","m-TOO, WAH-too"],["book, books","kitabu, vitabu","kee-TAH-boo, vee-TAH-boo"],["house, houses","nyumba, nyumba","NYOOM-bah, NYOOM-bah"],["tree, trees","mti, miti","m-TEE, MEE-tee"]],"ex":[["one house, houses","nyumba moja, nyumba nyingi","NYOOM-bah MOH-jah, NYOOM-bah NYEEN-gee"],["one book, books","kitabu kimoja, vitabu vingi","kee-TAH-boo kee-MOH-jah, vee-TAH-boo VEEN-gee"],["one cat, cats","paka mmoja, paka wengi","PAH-kah m-MOH-jah, PAH-kah WEN-gee"],["two books","vitabu viwili","vee-TAH-boo vee-WEE-lee"],["the children","watoto","wah-TOH-toh"]]},{"id":"to-be-ni","title":"To be: ni","text":["\"Ni\" is \"is / am / are\" for all persons. In the negative it becomes \"si\". For places use \"-ko\" with a prefix: niko (I am at)."],"rows":[["I am a teacher","mimi ni mwalimu","MEE-mee nee mwah-LEE-moo"],["this is a book","hiki ni kitabu","HEE-kee nee kee-TAH-boo"],["I am at home","niko nyumbani","NEE-koh nyoom-BAH-nee"],["I am tall","mimi ni mrefu","MEE-mee nee m-REH-foo"]],"ex":[["I am a student","mimi ni mwanafunzi","MEE-mee nee mwah-nah-FOON-zee"],["you are tired","umechoka","oo-meh-CHOH-kah"],["he is a doctor","yeye ni daktari","YEH-yeh nee dahk-TAH-ree"],["we are happy","tuna furaha","TOO-nah foo-RAH-hah"],["they are at home","wako nyumbani","WAH-koh nyoom-BAH-nee"]]},{"id":"having-na","title":"Having: -na","text":["Swahili says \"I am with\": ni- + na = nina (I have), una (you have), ana (he has), tuna (we have), mna (you have), wana (they have)."],"rows":[["I have","nina","NEE-nah"],["you have","una","OO-nah"],["he / she has","ana","AH-nah"],["we have","tuna","TOO-nah"],["I do not have","sina","SEE-nah"]],"ex":[["I have an older brother","nina kaka mkubwa","NEE-nah KAH-kah m-KOO-bwah"],["I have a car","nina gari","NEE-nah GAH-ree"],["I do not have time","sina muda","SEE-nah MOO-dah"],["there is a problem","kuna tatizo","KOO-nah tah-TEE-zoh"],["there is no water","hakuna maji","hah-KOO-nah MAH-jee"]]},{"id":"present-tense","title":"Present tense","text":["Verb = who + tense + stem. Present: -na-. Ni-na-soma (I am reading), u-na-soma (you), a-na-soma (he, she), tu-na-soma (we), m-na-soma (you plural), wa-na-soma (they)."],"rows":[["I read","ninasoma","nee-nah-SOH-mah"],["you read","unasoma","oo-nah-SOH-mah"],["he / she reads","anasoma","ah-nah-SOH-mah"],["we read","tunasoma","too-nah-SOH-mah"]],"ex":[["I am eating bread","ninakula mkate","nee-nah-KOO-lah m-KAH-teh"],["you are reading a book","unasoma kitabu","oo-nah-SOH-mah kee-TAH-boo"],["she works in a bank","anafanya kazi benki","ah-nah-FAHN-yah KAH-zee BEHN-kee"],["we drink tea","tunakunywa chai","too-nah-KOON-wah CHAH-ee"],["they are sleeping","wanalala","wah-nah-LAH-lah"]]},{"id":"basic-sentences","title":"Basic sentences","text":["The order is subject, verb, object. The verb already holds the subject."],"rows":[["I read a book","ninasoma kitabu","nee-nah-SOH-mah kee-TAH-boo"],["he drinks tea","anakunywa chai","ah-nah-KOON-wah CHAH-ee"],["a big house","nyumba kubwa","NYOOM-bah KOO-bwah"],["a new car","gari jipya","GAH-ree JEE-pyah"]],"ex":[["I read a book","ninasoma kitabu","nee-nah-SOH-mah kee-TAH-boo"],["he drinks tea","anakunywa chai","ah-nah-KOON-wah CHAH-ee"],["we go to school","tunakwenda shule","too-nah-KWEN-dah SHOO-leh"],["they eat bread","wanakula mkate","wah-nah-KOO-lah m-KAH-teh"],["the teacher writes","mwalimu anaandika","mwah-LEE-moo ah-nah-ahn-DEE-kah"]]},{"id":"negation","title":"Negation","text":["Add \"ha-\" at the front and change the tense marker. Present negative: ha- + prefix + verb ending in -i: sisomi (I do not read), husomi (you do not), hasomi (he does not)."],"rows":[["I do not go","siendi","see-EN-dee"],["you do not go","huendi","hoo-EN-dee"],["he / she does not go","haendi","hah-EN-dee"],["it is not good","si nzuri","see n-ZOO-ree"]],"ex":[["I want","nataka","nah-TAH-kah"],["I do not want","sitaki","see-TAH-kee"],["I speak English","ninazungumza Kiingereza","nee-nah-zoon-GOOM-zah kee-een-geh-REH-zah"],["I do not speak English","sizungumzi Kiingereza","see-zoon-GOOM-zee kee-een-geh-REH-zah"],["I like it","ninaipenda","nee-nah-ee-PEHN-dah"],["I do not like it","siipendi","see-ee-PEHN-dee"],["she is here","yuko hapa","YOO-koh HAH-pah"],["she is not here","hayuko hapa","hah-YOO-koh HAH-pah"],["I have a car","nina gari","NEE-nah GAH-ree"],["I do not have a car","sina gari","SEE-nah GAH-ree"],["I understand","naelewa","nah-eh-LEH-wah"],["I do not understand","sielewi","see-eh-LEH-wee"],["we are tired","tumechoka","too-meh-CHOH-kah"],["we are not tired","hatujachoka","hah-too-jah-CHOH-kah"],["he works on Sundays","anafanya kazi Jumapili","ah-nah-FAHN-yah KAH-zee joo-mah-PEE-lee"],["he does not work on Sundays","hafanyi kazi Jumapili","hah-FAHN-yee KAH-zee joo-mah-PEE-lee"]]},{"id":"asking-questions","title":"Asking questions","text":["The word order does not change. Raise your voice at the end. Or add \"je\" at the front, or \"au\" (or) at the end."],"rows":[["Do you go?","unaenda?","oo-nah-EHN-dah"],["Is it good?","ni nzuri?","nee n-ZOO-ree"],["Is it right?","si kweli?","see KWEH-lee"]],"ex":[["is this your book?","hiki ni kitabu chako?","HEE-kee nee kee-TAH-boo CHAH-koh"],["are they here?","wako hapa?","WAH-koh HAH-pah"],["do you like tea?","unapenda chai?","oo-nah-PEHN-dah CHAH-ee"],["is it cold?","kuna baridi?","KOO-nah bah-REE-dee"],["do you speak English?","unazungumza Kiingereza?","oo-nah-zoon-GOOM-zah kee-een-geh-REH-zah"]]},{"id":"question-words","title":"Question words","text":["Question words usually come at the end of the sentence."],"rows":[["who","nani","NAH-nee"],["what","nini","NEE-nee"],["where","wapi","WAH-pee"],["when","lini","LEE-nee"],["why","kwa nini","kwah NEE-nee"],["how","vipi","VEE-pee"],["how much","ngapi","NGAH-pee"]],"ex":[["what is your name?","jina lako nani?","JEE-nah LAH-koh NAH-nee"],["who is he?","yeye ni nani?","YEH-yeh nee NAH-nee"],["where do you live?","unaishi wapi?","oo-nah-EE-shee WAH-pee"],["when is the lesson?","somo ni lini?","SOH-moh nee LEE-nee"],["why are you late?","kwa nini umechelewa?","kwah NEE-nee oo-meh-cheh-LEH-wah"],["how much is it?","ni bei gani?","nee BEH-ee GAH-nee"],["which book?","kitabu kipi?","kee-TAH-boo KEE-pee"]]},{"id":"possessives-and-liking","title":"Possessives and liking","text":["The possessive agrees with the noun class: kitabu changu (my book), vitabu vyangu (my books), nyumba yangu (my house), mtoto wangu (my child). Your: -ako, his / her: -ake, our: -etu."],"rows":[["my book","kitabu changu","kee-TAH-boo CHAHN-goo"],["your book","kitabu chako","kee-TAH-boo CHAH-koh"],["his / her book","kitabu chake","kee-TAH-boo CHAH-keh"]],"ex":[["my phone","simu yangu","SEE-moo YAHN-goo"],["your house (formal)","nyumba yako","NYOOM-bah YAH-koh"],["his sister","dada yake","DAH-dah YAH-keh"],["I like music","ninapenda muziki","nee-nah-PEHN-dah moo-ZEE-kee"],["I love football","ninapenda mpira wa miguu","nee-nah-PEHN-dah m-PEE-rah wah mee-GOO"]]},{"id":"formal-vs-informal","title":"Formal vs informal","text":["Swahili shows respect with greetings and titles: \"shikamoo\" to elders, \"mzee\" for an older man, \"mama\" for a woman, \"bwana\" for sir. Use \"tafadhali\" when you ask for things."],"rows":[["respectful greeting to an elder","shikamoo","shee-kah-MOH"],["sir","bwana","BWAH-nah"],["madam","bibi","BEE-bee"]],"ex":[["how are you? (informal)","hujambo?","hoo-JAHM-boh"],["how are you? (formal)","habari za asubuhi?","hah-BAH-ree zah ah-soo-BOO-hee"],["where are you going? (informal)","unaenda wapi?","oo-nah-EHN-dah WAH-pee"],["where are you going? (formal)","unaelekea wapi, mzee?","oo-nah-eh-leh-KEH-ah WAH-pee, m-ZEH-eh"],["please sit down (formal)","tafadhali keti","tah-fah-DAH-lee KEH-tee"]]},{"id":"past-and-future-simple","title":"Past and future (simple)","text":["Past: -li-. Future: -ta-. Present perfect: -me-. Ni-li-soma (I read), ni-ta-soma (I will read), ni-me-soma (I have read)."],"rows":[["I ate","nilikula","nee-lee-KOO-lah"],["I will eat","nitakula","nee-tah-KOO-lah"],["I have eaten","nimekula","nee-meh-KOO-lah"],["I will go tomorrow","nitaenda kesho","nee-tah-EHN-dah KEH-shoh"]],"ex":[["yesterday I was tired","jana nilikuwa nimechoka","JAH-nah nee-lee-KOO-wah nee-meh-CHOH-kah"],["I will study tomorrow","nitasoma kesho","nee-tah-SOH-mah KEH-shoh"],["we went to the park","tulikwenda bustanini","too-lee-KWEN-dah boos-tah-NEE-nee"],["I saw him","nilimwona","nee-lee-m-WOH-nah"],["she wrote a letter","aliandika barua","ah-lee-ahn-DEE-kah bah-ROO-ah"]]},{"id":"commands","title":"Commands","text":["Use the bare verb stem for one person (soma!). For many people add -ni (someni!). To forbid, use \"usi-\" before the verb: usiende (do not go)."],"rows":[["come!","njoo!","N-joh-oh"],["wait!","subiri!","soo-BEE-ree"],["do not go","usiende","oo-see-EHN-deh"],["please wait","tafadhali subiri","tah-fah-DAH-lee soo-BEE-ree"]],"ex":[["come here","njoo hapa","N-joh-oh HAH-pah"],["do not come here","usije hapa","oo-SEE-jeh HAH-pah"],["sit down","keti","KEH-tee"],["do not sit down","usikae","oo-see-KAH-eh"],["be quiet","nyamaza","nyah-MAH-zah"],["do not be late","usichelewe","oo-see-cheh-LEH-weh"],["open the door","fungua mlango","foon-GOO-ah m-LAHN-goh"],["close the window","funga dirisha","FOON-gah dee-REE-shah"],["listen to me","nisikilize","nee-see-kee-LEE-zeh"],["do not worry","usiwe na wasiwasi","oo-SEE-weh nah wah-see-WAH-see"],["speak slowly","sema polepole","SEH-mah poh-leh-POH-leh"],["wait a moment","subiri kidogo","soo-BEE-ree kee-DOH-goh"]]},{"id":"can-must-want","title":"Can, must, want","text":["\"Kuweza\" (can), \"kutaka\" (want) and \"lazima\" (must) go before the main verb. Swahili uses the infinitive: naweza kuogelea (I can swim)."],"rows":[["I can swim","naweza kuogelea","nah-WEH-zah koo-oh-geh-LEH-ah"],["I must go","lazima niende","lah-ZEE-mah nee-EHN-deh"],["I want to go","nataka kwenda","nah-TAH-kah KWEN-dah"],["may I?","naweza?","nah-WEH-zah"]],"ex":[["I can swim","naweza kuogelea","nah-WEH-zah koo-oh-geh-LEH-ah"],["I cannot swim","siwezi kuogelea","see-WEH-zee koo-oh-geh-LEH-ah"],["can you help me?","unaweza kunisaidia?","oo-nah-WEH-zah koo-nee-sah-ee-DEE-ah"],["we must go","lazima twende","lah-ZEE-mah TWEN-deh"],["we must not go","hatupaswi kwenda","hah-too-PAHS-wee KWEN-dah"],["I want to eat","nataka kula","nah-TAH-kah KOO-lah"],["I do not want to eat","sitaki kula","see-TAH-kee KOO-lah"],["you can come","unaweza kuja","oo-nah-WEH-zah KOO-jah"],["you cannot come","huwezi kuja","hoo-WEH-zee KOO-jah"],["she wants to study","anataka kusoma","ah-nah-TAH-kah koo-SOH-mah"],["I must work today","lazima nifanye kazi leo","lah-ZEE-mah nee-FAHN-yeh KAH-zee LEH-oh"],["you must not run","hupaswi kukimbia","hoo-PAHS-wee koo-keem-BEE-ah"]]},{"id":"in-on-at","title":"In, on, at","text":["Swahili uses \"-ni\" at the end of a noun for \"in / at\": nyumbani (at home), shuleni (at school). Or use \"juu ya\" (on), \"chini ya\" (under), \"karibu na\" (near), \"kando ya\" (next to)."],"rows":[["at home","nyumbani","nyoom-BAH-nee"],["at school","shuleni","shoo-LEH-nee"],["on the table","juu ya meza","JOO yah MEH-zah"],["under the table","chini ya meza","CHEE-nee yah MEH-zah"]],"ex":[["the book is on the table","kitabu kiko juu ya meza","kee-TAH-boo KEE-koh JOO yah MEH-zah"],["the cat is under the table","paka yuko chini ya meza","PAH-kah YOO-koh CHEE-nee yah MEH-zah"],["I am at school","niko shuleni","NEE-koh shoo-LEH-nee"],["I am at home","niko nyumbani","NEE-koh nyoom-BAH-nee"],["the shop is next to the bank","duka liko kando ya benki","DOO-kah LEE-koh KAHN-doh yah BEHN-kee"],["the park is near the station","bustani iko karibu na kituo","boos-TAH-nee EE-koh kah-REE-boo nah kee-TOH-oh"],["we meet in the morning","tunakutana asubuhi","too-nah-koo-TAH-nah ah-soo-BOO-hee"],["the lesson is at nine","somo ni saa tatu","SOH-moh nee SAH-ah TAH-too"],["the key is in the bag","ufunguo uko mfukoni","oo-foon-GOO-oh OO-koh m-foo-KOH-nee"]]},{"id":"comparing-things","title":"Comparing things","text":["There is no -er ending. Use \"zaidi ya\" (more than) after the adjective: kubwa zaidi ya (bigger than). For \"the most\", say \"kuliko wote\" (than all)."],"rows":[["big, bigger","kubwa, kubwa zaidi","KOO-bwah, KOO-bwah ZAH-ee-dee"],["good, better","nzuri, nzuri zaidi","n-ZOO-ree, n-ZOO-ree ZAH-ee-dee"],["the biggest","kubwa kuliko wote","KOO-bwah koo-LEE-koh WOH-teh"]],"ex":[["big, bigger, the biggest","kubwa, kubwa zaidi, kubwa kuliko zote","KOO-bwah, KOO-bwah ZAH-ee-dee, KOO-bwah koo-LEE-koh ZOH-teh"],["small, smaller, the smallest","ndogo, ndogo zaidi, ndogo kuliko zote","N-doh-goh, N-doh-goh ZAH-ee-dee, N-doh-goh koo-LEE-koh ZOH-teh"],["this is better than that","hii ni bora kuliko ile","HEE nee BOH-rah koo-LEE-koh EE-leh"],["this is worse than that","hii ni mbaya kuliko ile","HEE nee M-bah-yah koo-LEE-koh EE-leh"],["she is taller than me","yeye ni mrefu kuliko mimi","YEH-yeh nee m-REH-foo koo-LEE-koh MEE-mee"],["Tashkent is bigger than Samarkand","Tashkent ni kubwa kuliko Samarkand","tahsh-KENT nee KOO-bwah koo-LEE-koh sah-mar-KAHND"],["it is the cheapest","ni nafuu kuliko zote","nee nah-FOO koo-LEE-koh ZOH-teh"],["the same as","sawa na","SAH-wah nah"]]},{"id":"everyday-sentences","title":"Everyday sentences","text":["Quick sentences to copy and change."],"rows":[["I am hungry","nina njaa","NEE-nah N-jah-ah"],["I am thirsty","nina kiu","NEE-nah KEE-oo"],["I am cold","nina baridi","NEE-nah bah-REE-dee"],["it is raining","mvua inanyesha","m-VOO-ah ee-nah-NYEH-shah"]],"ex":[["he is a teacher","yeye ni mwalimu","YEH-yeh nee mwah-LEE-moo"],["you (plural) are students","ninyi ni wanafunzi","NEE-nyee nee wah-nah-FOON-zee"],["I am happy","nina furaha","NEE-nah foo-RAH-hah"],["she is at school","yuko shuleni","YOO-koh shoo-LEH-nee"],["you are my friend","wewe ni rafiki yangu","WEH-weh nee rah-FEE-kee YAHN-goo"],["it is cold","kuna baridi","KOO-nah bah-REE-dee"],["I study English","ninasoma Kiingereza","nee-nah-SOH-mah kee-een-geh-REH-zah"],["he teaches maths","anafundisha hisabati","ah-nah-foon-DEE-shah hee-sah-BAH-tee"],["they work every day","wanafanya kazi kila siku","wah-nah-FAHN-yah KAH-zee KEE-lah SEE-koo"],["is this your book?","hiki ni kitabu chako?","HEE-kee nee kee-TAH-boo CHAH-koh"],["are they here?","wako hapa?","WAH-koh HAH-pah"],["do you like tea?","unapenda chai?","oo-nah-PEHN-dah CHAH-ee"],["what time is it?","saa ngapi?","SAH-ah NGAH-pee"],["whose book is this?","hiki ni kitabu cha nani?","HEE-kee nee kee-TAH-boo chah NAH-nee"],["how old are you?","una umri gani?","OO-nah OOM-ree GAH-nee"],["how do you say it?","inasemwaje?","ee-nah-SEM-wah-jeh"],["your book (formal)","kitabu chako","kee-TAH-boo CHAH-koh"],["their house","nyumba yao","NYOOM-bah YAH-oh"],["my phone","simu yangu","SEE-moo YAHN-goo"],["excuse me, sir","samahani, bwana","sah-mah-HAH-nee, BWAH-nah"],["please sit down (formal)","tafadhali keti","tah-fah-DAH-lee KEH-tee"],["come here (informal)","njoo hapa","N-joh-oh HAH-pah"],["yesterday I was tired","jana nilikuwa nimechoka","JAH-nah nee-lee-KOO-wah nee-meh-CHOH-kah"],["I will study tomorrow","nitasoma kesho","nee-tah-SOH-mah KEH-shoh"],["we went to the park","tulikwenda bustanini","too-lee-KWEN-dah boos-tah-NEE-nee"]]}],"name":"Swahili","id":"sw","flag":"ke","note":""}